 "steps": [
  {
   "caption": "Step 1, the sign: 13.625 is positive, so the sign bit is 0.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l1",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Step 2, the integer part in binary: 13 = 8 + 4 + 1 = 1101₂.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l2",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Step 3, the fraction part by repeated doubling: 0.625 × 2 = 1.25 (bit 1), 0.25 × 2 = 0.5 (bit 0), 0.5 × 2 = 1.0 (bit 1). So 0.625 = 0.101₂, and it terminates.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l3",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Step 4, normalise: move the point 3 places left so exactly one 1 is before it. 1101.101₂ = 1.101101₂ × 2³.",
   "patches": [
    {
     "id": "l4",
     "set": {
      "hidden": false
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "caption": "Step 5, bias the exponent: e = 3 + 127 = 130 = 10000010₂.",
